@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title The unit baseline, retired — guest-lib tests run in the Linux lane
' purpose: why the unit suite needs no skip list, and how a macOS host runs the tests that drive the guest shell lib
' covers: mise.toml
' covers: internal/contract/mise_gates_test.go
' covers: internal/testx/linux_lane.go
'   the decision ............ _spec/_plans/tui-upgrades-delivery.puml (DECISIONS, D12)
'   the full gate ........... _spec/_devops/release-gate.puml
'   the lib under test ...... _spec/internal/sbx/state-sync.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
' status: RETIRED 2026-11-25. `mise run test` has no --baseline flag and
' mise.toml has no [vars] unit_baseline. TestUnitLaneRunsEveryTest keeps
' them out.
'
' ── WHAT THE BASELINE WAS (2026-11-10 to 2026-11-25) ─────────────────────
' `go test ./...` was red on macOS before any change, so a branch could not
' tell old red from new. The Executor chose "no new failing tests" on
' 2026-11-10: `mise run test --baseline` added
'   -skip='^(<[vars] unit_baseline>)$'
' over a sorted list of top-level test names. It grew to 25 rows: 24 macOS
' tooling failures and one flake.
'
' ── WHY THE ROWS WERE RED (MEASURED 2026-11-25, darwin/arm64) ─────────────
' 22 rows drive packages/lib/*.sh, which targets the Linux guest. macOS gave
' them /bin/bash 3.2 and BSD tools: no find -printf, no cp --parents -t, no
' xargs -d, no mv -T, no flock, and bash 3.2 counts an emoji in bytes.
' The same tests passed in golang:1.26.7 (Debian, bash 5.2) and in
' proveo/base-node:local (Ubuntu 26.04, bash 5.3, node 22): 22 of 22.
' TestOpenCodeSeedProgressFixtures already passed on macOS; its row was stale.
' TestAdbMirrorStartsWithTheSocketAddress slept a fixed 50ms before reading a
' background stub's log. It now polls for the line it expects, up to 5s.
'
' ── THE LINUX LANE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' A guest-lib test starts with `if testx.InLinux(t) { return }`.
'   linux host ........ returns false; the test runs in place
'   other host ........ go test -c for GOOS=linux once per package, then
'                       docker run proveo/base-node:local with the module
'                       mounted read-only at its own path, --network none,
'                       -run '^<TestName>$'; a FAIL fails the host test and a
'                       SKIP inside skips it
'   no docker/image ... t.Skip naming what is missing
' PROVEO_LINUX_LANE=inside marks the delegated run; PROVEO_LINUX_LANE_IMAGE
' picks another image. Both are registered in internal/envreg.
' MEASURED 2026-11-25: `go test -count=1 -race ./...` passed on this macOS
' host with no skip list; internal/contract plus internal/sbx took about 16s.
' NOT CHOSEN: Homebrew GNU tools (host change, drifts from the guest);
' porting the lib to bash 3.2 and BSD (rewrites the guest copy path); a
' linux build tag (the tests would never run on a Mac).

component """mise run test\ngo test -race -cover ./...""" as RUN <<app>>
component "guest-lib test\nif testx.InLinux(t)" as LIBTEST <<app>>
node "proveo/base-node:local\nbash 5.3 · GNU · flock · node" as IMAGE <<host>>
component "[vars] unit_baseline\n25 rows · RETIRED" as LIST <<error>>
component "no Docker or image\nt.Skip, named" as SKIP <<async>>

RUN ARROW_MAIN LIBTEST
LIBTEST ARROW_MAIN IMAGE : off Linux
LIBTEST ARROW_OPTIONAL SKIP : nothing to run it in
LIST ARROW_ERROR RUN : no -skip remains

note bottom of LIST
  **A skip list hides drift as well as red.**
  Every row now passes on its target toolchain,
  so the list and the flag that read it are gone.
end note

note bottom of IMAGE
  **The lane runs the guest's own toolchain.**
  Testing the lib under macOS tools measured the
  host, not the code that ships into the sandbox.
end note

note bottom of SKIP
  **A missing image is a skip, not a pass.**
  The message names Docker or the build command,
  so a Mac without either still reads honestly.
end note
@enduml
